A||||0||gtsonly||A word to the wise-Hydraulic lifters!!!!||||6||
Z||000000||gtsonly||12-25-2001||06:54 PM||||Mind you, I am an aircraft mech and have been one for 12 years but I just rebuilt the 2.8 in my GT and followed the Haynes(sucks) manual. I replaced the lifters (first time with hydraulic lifters) and the Haynes(sucks) manual does not refer to priming the lifters. My problem was after the lash and engine back together, I had no compression. As I have come to find after the engine has turned over a few times the lifters prime themselves and low and behold the valves are all open, hence no compression. I had to re-lash the valves. Many might know this, but it was a first for me. To prime the lifters prior to installing, place them in a cup of oil and use the pushrod and pump them up full of oil. Hope this helps some people<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/myfiero001_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||6
